# Design

- Guard key: the overlay route token. It is set in one place, `overlay[ROUTE_TOKEN_KEY] = self._remember(selection)` (`cielairouter_gateway_overlay.py:249` in the working tree), and `apply` returns other providers' configs unchanged (`if provider != PROVIDER ...: return pcfg`, line 206). `discovery_provider_config` pops the token. So the check needs no provider-name comparison. It is the same data-marker pattern these modules already use for `REMOTE_BRIDGE_CONFIG_MARKER`.
- Why a replay would reuse the same gateway: `openai_forwarding` computes `url` once (line 157) and `reopen_initial_stream` passes that `url` and the same `pcfg` back to `open_with_retry`. The collection loop reuses its `url` and `pcfg` argument on every attempt. The tests record the route token seen by each open. Before the fix the second open carried the same token: `['r1', 'r1']`.
- No retries were added. The only effect is that two existing replay windows close for routed configs. A selected route falls through to the same path that `stream_initial_retries: 0` (openai_forwarding) or an exhausted truncation budget (collection: `*_stream_read_exhausted` log, `UpstreamStreamReadError(attempts=1)`) already uses.
- The change makes no assumption that a `URLError`, a reset or an empty stream is safe to replay.

# Difference from the existing upstream_retry helper

`upstream_retry._selected_cielairouter_gateway` also requires `provider == "cielairouter"`. The new helper checks only the token, so this task adds no provider-name branch. Unconfirmed edge case: if a non-CielAiRouter provider's config.json held a literal `ciel_gateway_route` key, that provider would also lose these two replays. I found no code path that produces such a config.

# Reachability (verified, limits the claim)

[`protocol-selection-probe.txt`](retry-boundaries-evidence/protocol-selection-probe.txt): `select_provider_protocol("cielairouter", ...)` returns `anthropic_messages` for `anthropic_messages`, `openai_responses` for `openai_responses`, and `openai_chat` for `openai_chat`. This holds for `native_compat` unset, true and false.

- `claude_router.py` calls `forward_openai_compatible_chat` only when the `anthropic_messages` selection yields `openai_chat`.
- `ResponseCollectionContext.collect` collects only for `ollama_chat`, `openai_chat` and `anthropic_messages` after selecting for `openai_responses`.
- So with the current adapter, CielAiRouter Claude Code and Codex requests reach neither guarded site. The guard is a boundary for any routed config that does reach them. It does not change the native Responses path in the 9385 TLS-EOF investigation; that path is `provider_responses_passthrough.py`, owned by another agent.

# Unchanged (verified by test or code reading as noted)

- CielAiRouter config without a token (`discovery_provider_config` of an overlay copy): 2 opens and recovery on the initial stream; 2 opens and success on collection truncation. Verified by test.
- Other providers (`openai`, `alitoken`): initial reconnect and one truncation retry, unchanged. Verified by new and existing tests.
- Kimi capacity/transport retries, remote-bridge zero-retry policy, the runaway re-issue ladder (`collect_without_runaway`, which re-asks after a completed looped collection, not after a transport failure), and `open_with_retry` 429/key-rotation handling are not touched. Code reading.

